Example
Let 𝐴= {1, 2, 3} and 𝑅= {(𝑎, 𝑏) | 𝑎≤𝑏}
What are the elements of 𝑅?
Note 𝑅is a relation from 𝐴to 𝐴.
𝑅= {(1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3), (2, 2), (2, 3), (3, 3)}𝐴= {1, 2, 3} and 𝐴
= {1, 2, 3}

Combining Relations
• Since relations from 𝐴to 𝐵are subset of 𝐴× 𝐵, two relations 
from 𝐴to 𝐵can be combined through set operations
• Let 𝐴= {1, 2, 3} and 𝐵= {1, 2, 3, 4}. The relations 
𝑅1 = {(1, 1), (2, 2), (3, 3)} and
𝑅2 = {(1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4)} can be combined to obtain:
𝑅1 ∪𝑅2 = {(1, 1), (1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4), (2,2), (3, 3)}
𝑅1 ∩𝑅2 = {(1, 1)}
𝑅1 – 𝑅2 = {(2, 2), (3, 3)}
𝑅2 – 𝑅1 = {(1, 2), (1, 3), (1, 4)}

Reflexive Closure
• Example:
Let A = {1, 2, 3, 4} and the relation R on A
R = {(1, 1), (2, 2), (4, 4)}
Then by the definition of a reflexive closure:
S = R ∪{(x, x) | x ∈A } = {(1, 1), (2, 2), (4, 4), (3, 3)}

Symmetric Closure
• Example:
Let 𝐴= {1, 2, 3} and the relation on 𝑅on 𝐴
𝑅= {(1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 2)}
Then by the definition of a symmetric closure:
𝑆= 𝑅∪{(𝑎, 𝑏) | (𝑏, 𝑎) ∈𝑅} = {(1, 2), (2, 3), (3, 2), (2,1)}
